    {
      "id": "D1",
      "plan_ref": "plan.html section 5 baseline protocol / A1",
      "text": "The >=10x workload-scaling suggestion is WITHDRAWN. External microsecond timing already gives compute >> 1 ms (117/221/33 ms), and scaling would change the pinned constants and therefore the checksum-verified RESULT lines, which section 2 non-goal #7 forbids. Constants stay pinned."
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "plan_ref": "A2 / section 6 #14",
      "text": "BENCH_ITERS / BENCH_FLOORS rows are NOT added in Phase 0. Literal A2 is a No-Go: benchmarks/map.matrix and benchmarks/json.matrix already exist as two of the 8 gated workloads, so the stems collide; adding new floors would make `bench --gate --compare --runs 5` gate 11 workloads on shared CI runners with no pinned-host calibration. src/cli.rs is untouched (zero diff) and the 8 gated workloads are exactly preserved. Floors are re-baselined in Phase 4 with a pinned host and recorded rationale. The new harness reports iters/sec itself, so rate reporting is preserved."
    },
    {
      "id": "D3",
      "plan_ref": "A2 / section 10",
      "text": "tools/gate.sh and tools/difftest.sh are NOT wired into the 3-OS CI matrix. gate.sh builds native+gui (LLVM 18 + webkit, absent on ubuntu/macos runners) and difftest.sh hardcodes target/debug/spid3r.exe with no cross-platform binary detection; both would turn CI red. Both are run locally TWICE in the DoD gate sequence. A new additive ubuntu-only `phase0` CI job runs the blocking manifest/fixture verifiers and self-test instead."
    },
    {
      "id": "D4",
      "plan_ref": "section 6 #2",
      "text": "The 3 HLC fixtures join the differential set via ADDITIVE golden-value Case rows in tests/engine_matrix.rs (exact expected stdout, exit code, stderr) and a NEW read-only verifier, with NO edits to any existing gate and NO stdout normalization inside an existing gate. No scoped contract deviation is required."
    }
  ],
